{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1510552-advice-on-a-odd-titan-cult-idea","id":1510552,"title":"Advice on a odd Titan Cult idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-02T20:47:20-07:00","id":1510552,"title":"Advice on a odd Titan Cult idea","content":"While brainstorming antagonists for a Scion idea I came up with the beginnings of an interesting, but odd one. The Chivalric Order of Ashwood Hall is a modern-day Chivalric order founded in the Victorian Era by Sir Winslow Morris, a tea magnate, and secret Titan cultist. Haven't determined the Cult's main function, but they are currently a secret society of basically modern-day Black Knights and Dark Paladins, complete with actual sets of combat-ready plate armour. They either serve Apep, Isfet, or another Titan ruthlessly, using their connections to further whatever goal said Titan is pushing.<br /> <br /> Can I have some advice on making this idea work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T07:12:18-07:00","id":1510590,"title":"","content":"This is a great idea! A lot of the Victorians were really into Egyptian stuff so it makes sense. I think Apep would be a perfect Titan for an order of dark knights to serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T07:21:35-07:00","id":1510593,"title":"","content":"I agree a Victorian occultist group with an interest in the Egyptian pantheon makes sense.<br /> <br /> But why are they serving a Titan? The Victorian aristocracy was obsessed with order, so serving Titans linked with disorder doesn't immediately make sense. What's their belief system? What are they getting out of it for themselves? Do they believe Apep's eventual victory is inevitable and that, if they serve him, they will reign by his side in the resulting Chaos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T14:32:57-07:00","id":1510639,"title":"","content":"Upon more reflection, I would suggest either Cronus of the Theoi or Aten of the Netjer as the focus of the Titan cult. Their all-consuming desire for domination is a good fit with the absolute worst aspects of the Victorian aristocracy. They are both from pantheons that the Victorians would be familiar with and respect. And they both could be dressed up in a guise of respectability--in his Roman Mantle of Saturn, Cronus was actually seen as a benign ruler of the Golden Age; and Aten promotes monotheism (his monotheism).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T04:29:36-07:00","id":1510972,"title":"","content":"Aten sounds like a good choice, if we stick to the whole Egyptomania angle. Though there is a question of whether or not the cult sees itself as the &quot;Black Knights&quot; or &quot;the True Defenders/Rulers of the Realm&quot;. Aten is a poor choice for black knights....but honestly, that isn't a Titan's role in Egyptian myths, that is Seth/Set/Sutekh's.<br /> Apep the Titan (as opposed to the Dragon of the Joka flight) is associated with Chaos and, well hunger. We'd be looking at more, hedonistic Knights, like the Ashwood Abby.<br /> Isfet is closer to Deception but is also chaotic. I'd lean towards the Knights Templar from Assassin's Creed series, if not the Assassin's themselves.<br /> Aten DOES ALREADY have something resembling an order of Knights. The Order of the Revealing Light (listed on Titanomachy pg 40) was formerly a group of Crusaders who Aten...recruited. Though they have largely abandoned that role by modern day.<br /> <br /> I think the first step to work out how the cult fulfils the role is, of course asking who do they serve.<br /> <br /> If they are meant to be a paramilitarys in plate mail, then we need to know if that is their normal day to day thing, or if it is their &quot;oh SH#T, the boss just gave us a priority mission, puill out all the stops&quot;.kinda deal. Honestly, not sure what you want from the group;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T07:56:42-07:00","id":1515742,"title":"","content":"I had some vague ideas for titans, but more along the lines of demonization of older gods, and writing up how they were originally. Looking at the Greek titans.<br /> it's an idea separate from how titans are defined by Scion. There's so much unknown, and like an empty bucket seems to demand to be filled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T15:48:06-07:00","id":1515795,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t worry too much about the cult\u2019s goals and objectives matching up with the Titan they worship. It\u2019s a common trope for cultist to summon their god only to be consumed/destroyed by it because they called to understand what they were worshiping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T11:10:56-07:00","id":1516354,"title":"","content":"As an alternative, the cult is dedicated to a Titan incarnation that uses the Motif of the Arthurian Black Knight, invoking the Motif to gain power. Since it's an incarnation you don't even need to reveal which Titan it actually is (but Bres would be a good choice).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.medievalchronicles.com/medieval-knights/famous-medieval-knights/the-black-knight/\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Knight (medievalchronicles.com)</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}